course: dictionary
lesson: 10426
title: Meet the trombone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word you do not know can often be understood from the words around it. Here the context is about music. «Brass players buzz their lips into the mouthpiece; the trumpet, trombone, horn and tuba are brass.» The sentence lists instruments together, so a trombone must be a musical instrument from the same family as the trumpet.
explain: Read on to find more clues. A trombone is a large brass instrument. You play it by blowing into it and moving a long sliding tube in and out, which changes the notes. The word «sliding» is a clue to how it works: the tube slides, it does not press keys.
explain: A person who plays the trombone is called a trombonist. In a band or orchestra, the trombonists play together with the other brass players. When you meet a new word in a list, ask yourself what the other words have in common. That is often the key.
fact: A trombone is a large brass musical instrument.
fact: You play a trombone by blowing into it and moving a long sliding tube in and out.
fact: Moving the slide changes the notes you play.
fact: A person who plays the trombone is a trombonist.
fact: «Brass players buzz their lips into the mouthpiece; the trumpet, trombone, horn and tuba are brass.» So the trumpet, trombone, horn and tuba are all brass instruments.
fact: The trombone plays low notes, and it is often heard in bands and orchestras.
exercise: What do you do to play a trombone? | Pluck its strings with your fingers | *Blow into it and slide a long tube in and out | Press keys to make a sound | Hit it with sticks
exercise: «The trumpet, trombone, horn and tuba are brass.» What family do these instruments belong to? | Keyboards | Percussion | *Brass | Strings
exercise: What is a person who plays the trombone called? | *Trombonist | Trombonella | Trombonic | Trombonaut
test: What makes the notes change on a trombone? | Turning a small dial | *Moving the long sliding tube in and out | Pressing a row of keys | Changing the strings
test: In cartoons, the «sad trombone» sound is used for what? | A sunrise | *A failure | A wedding | A birthday
exam: The trombone belongs to which family of instruments? | *Brass | Percussion | Strings | Woodwind
